Translational symmetry requires particle–hole bilinears to be diagonal in momentum. At each \(k\), the resulting \(2\times2\) Hermitian spin-density matrix has one charge component and three spin components; these exhaust all number-conserving Hartree–Fock order parameters. Thus,

\[
\boxed{
\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)+c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)-c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)+c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
-i\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)-c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)\right\rangle
}
\]

Translational symmetry restricts particle-hole bilinears to equal momenta. The four Hermitian components of the resulting spin density matrix exhaust all possible order parameters:

\[
\boxed{
\left\langle c^\dagger_\uparrow(k)c_\uparrow(k)\right\rangle+
\left\langle c^\dagger_\downarrow(k)c_\downarrow(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c^\dagger_\uparrow(k)c_\uparrow(k)\right\rangle-
\left\langle c^\dagger_\downarrow(k)c_\downarrow(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c^\dagger_\uparrow(k)c_\downarrow(k)\right\rangle+
\left\langle c^\dagger_\downarrow(k)c_\uparrow(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
-i\left\langle c^\dagger_\uparrow(k)c_\downarrow(k)\right\rangle+
i\left\langle c^\dagger_\downarrow(k)c_\uparrow(k)\right\rangle
}
\]

Under translation by a lattice vector \(n\), \(c_s^\dagger(k_1)c_{s'}(k_2)\) acquires the phase \(e^{i(k_1-k_2)\cdot n}\). Translational invariance therefore requires \(k_1=k_2\) modulo a reciprocal-lattice vector. Since Hartree–Fock decoupling is number conserving, the allowed order parameters are precisely the four components of the momentum-diagonal spin density matrix. The two spin-flip components are Hermitian conjugates.

\[
\boxed{
\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c_{\uparrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\downarrow}(k)\right\rangle
\;;\;
\left\langle c_{\downarrow}^{\dagger}(k)c_{\uparrow}(k)\right\rangle
}
\]

